e separate pins. I'll follow the SCUD's \\\"tied together\\\" if it explicitly says so, but usually it means they are all decoupled. Let's look at line 95 again: \\\"AVDD, CVDD, DVDD are internal regulator outputs tied together and decoupled to GND.\\\" This is a bit unusual for these ICs but I will follow SCUD.\\n\\nActually, looking at BQ79616 datasheet, AVDD, CVDD, DVDD are separate. I'll check the schematic images if possible, but I can't \\\"see\\\" them. I'll stick to SCUD.\\n\\nWait, I should check the pin names for U1. SCUD mentions some:\\nBAT (Pin 1)\\nAVDD, CVDD, DVDD\\nTSREF (Pin 51)\\nLDOIN (Pin 47)\\nNEG5V (Pin 44)\\nNPNB (Pin 48)\\nREFHP (Pin 37)\\nRX (Pin 52)\\nTX (Pin 53)\\nNFAULT (Pin 62)\\nBBP (Pin 64)\\nBBN (Pin 63)\\nVC0-VC16\\nCB0-CB16\\nGPIO1-GPIO8\\nAVSS, CVSS, DVSS, REFHM, PAD (GND)\\n\\nI'll use these names.\\n\\nLet's start.\"}",
